":null,"result":"I added the \"Async Stats\" component in `AsyncStatsComponent.cs`, and `dotnet build` succeeds with 0 errors. The only warnings are two NuGet notices that a slightly newer Grasshopper 8.0 package was used than the version range names. I haven't run it inside Grasshopper.\n\nThe project had no existing async pattern to copy, so I followed the setup of `AddComponent` (a `GH_Component` subclass with category \"Bench\", subcategory \"Data\") and added the background work myself.\n\n- **Inputs and outputs:** Values (list of numbers) goes in; Mean and StdDev come out.\n- **Not blocking the UI:** when the inputs change, the component cancels any computation still running and starts a new one on a background thread. While it runs, the component shows \"Computing...\". When it finishes, it refreshes itself on the UI thread and outputs the stored results.\n- **Choices I made:**\n  - **StdDev type:** it's the population standard deviation (dividing by n), not the sample one.\n  - **Empty list:** an empty list gives a \"No values provided\" warning instead of a number.\n  - **Multiple branches:** if the input is a data tree, each branch gets its own Mean and StdDev.\n  - **Cleanup:** a running computation is also cancelled when the component is deleted or the document is closed.","ttft_ms":3032,"type":"result","duration_ms":41059,"uuid":"bfb4c1ce-cae9-404a-9386-cf5e7f9b58ae","ttft_stream_ms":1951,"time_to_request_ms":251,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":3,"system_prompt":143,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":12,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"tool_pool_refresh":3,"init_message":40,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":2,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":5,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":18,"message_normalization":1,"client_creation":5,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":71,"time_